    "created_at": "2017-05-09T09:55:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-09T09:55:18Z",
    "body": "Not sure I understand the issue here. Which \"scripting is disabled\" are we talking about? Some user setting or non-current-Window objects? \r\n\r\nBut neither of those is bound to tab groups in Gecko (and I think tab group is what this new agent cluster is. (that 'agent' is for some reason really hard for me to understand in this context. ))\r\nWhen window object goes away, dedicated workers get killed, and shared too, if there aren't more windows keeping them alive.\r\n\r\nNote, if a page enters bfcache, that does not kill workers but freezes them.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
